{"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","title":"inDegree(of:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inDegree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V8inDegree2ofS2i_tF","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L219","fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift"},"modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"role":"symbol"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of columns with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" among their targets. O(1), cached."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/indegree(of:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/inDegree(of:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inDegree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"vertex","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a source"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"kind"